<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:41Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>CAS reinstates Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3682d798b784106e78a1cf89ef62fcfe8882a5b3766ebc9611ac2c9633bc41b0</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027--561a21777065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has reinstated Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions, overturning a CAF decision that stripped them of the title. Morocco, previously declared winners, are confirmed runners-up.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
